12. What are the three steps of the Von Neumann Architecture?
Fetch: the CPU gets the next instruction form the computer's memory using a location tracker (program counter)

Decode: The control unit breaks down and reads the instruction to figure out what command or action needs to be done

Execute: The Srithmetic logic unit (ALU) or another part of the CPU perfomrs the actual operation such as moving data or math calculations

